      "string" : "function.\nIn Banerjee [1992], agents observe only the actions of their predeces-\nsors. The Avery and Zemsky [1998] model adds a market maker who up-\ndates prices. See Lee [2021] for heterogeneous priors. Following Smith and\nSørensen [2000], we allow unbounded signals. Equilibrium notions are taken\nfrom Osborne and Rubinstein [1994], and the voting application follows the\nsequential procedure of Dekel and Piccione [2000].\n2 Model\nConsider a sequence of agents i= 1,2,... who each observe a private signal\nsi and the history of actions hi. The posterior belief satisfies\nµi =\nπf(si |H)\nπf(si |H) + (1−π)f(si |L). (1)\nProposition 1 states that an information cascade begins with positive proba-\nbility. The proof follows Bikhchandani et al. [1992] with minor modifications.\nItiseasytoseethattheinequalityispreservedwhenbothsidesaremultiplied\nby the likelihood ratio.\n3 Results\nTable 2 reports the estimates; the posterior in (1) is evaluated at the sample\nmean of the signal.\n2"
